course: dictionary
lesson: 7026
title: A people's name
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of people, and they often start with a capital letter. «Parsi» is the name of a group of people in India. Look at the clues around it: they came from Persia, which is now called Iran, and they follow the Zoroastrian religion.
explain: The story «How the Rhinoceros Got His Skin» uses an older spelling, «Parsee». A Parsee man lives on «an uninhabited island», which means an island where nobody lives. Parsee and Parsi are two spellings of the same word.
explain: Parsi can also describe things. A Parsi family belongs to this community, so Parsi is an adjective there. Ask yourself: is the word naming a person, or describing something? That tells you which meaning you need.
fact: Parsi is a noun for a person from this community. The plural is Parsis.
fact: Parsi is also an adjective, meaning belonging to this community.
fact: Parsee is an older spelling, and Parsi is the spelling used today.
fact: Parsis live mostly around Mumbai in India, and they are known for their fire temples.
fact: «Uninhabited» means with no people living there.
exercise: Parsi is a name for a people. Their ancestors came to India long ago from which country? | *Persia, now called Iran | Egypt | India | Russia
exercise: «The Parsi family visited their fire temple.» What kind of word is Parsi here? | *An adjective describing the family | A verb about moving | A noun naming a person | A place where people sleep
exercise: «An uninhabited island» means what? | An island that is always sunny | *An island where nobody lives | An island full of cake | An island with a big market
test: Parsis follow which religion? | *Zoroastrianism | Hinduism | Islam | Buddhism
test: Where do most Parsis live in India? | On the Red Sea shore | Around Delhi, the capital | In the Himalayas | *Mostly around Mumbai
exam: Parsee and Parsi are | two kinds of fire temple | two countries in Asia | *two spellings of the same word | two different peoples
